{"name":"Charismatic Red","hex":"#ee2244","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"charismatic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, related to, or having charisma: having a form of compelling charm or personality which inspires devotion in others; charming, fascinating, magnetic.","Of, related to, or being a member of a form of Christianity that emphasizes the role of the Holy Spirit."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Charismatic Movement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charismatic"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Charisma","blocks":[{"text":"Charisma is a personal quality of magnetic charm, persuasion, or appeal."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charisma","wikidata":"Q118157"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca